Windows 11 KB5127648: 802.1X / PEAP / MS-CHAPv2 Authentication Failure
Overview

Microsoft released KB5127648 on October 13, 2026 for Windows 11 versions 24H2, 25H2, and 26H2, corresponding to OS Builds 26100.9711, 26200.9711, and 26300.9711 respectively.

Following deployment of the October 2026 security updates, some enterprise devices can experience authentication failures with network connections that depend on MS-CHAPv2-based authentication, including:

Enterprise Wi-Fi
Wired 802.1X
PEAP-MSCHAPv2
EAP-MSCHAPv2
Some VPN connections

Microsoft documents this as the result of an intentional NTLMv1 security-hardening change introduced with Windows updates released on or after October 13, 2026.

Important: The registry configuration documented here should be considered a temporary compatibility mitigation, not a permanent security solution.

