Disclaimer

This documentation describes a temporary compatibility mitigation for environments confirmed to be affected by the October 2026 authentication-hardening changes.

Setting BlockNtlmv1SSO to 0 reduces enforcement of the security behavior introduced by the update and should not be considered a permanent security configuration. Test the change on a controlled device group before broad production deployment.

Documentation approach

I structured this so it works directly as a GitHub README.md: symptoms and root cause first, then confirmation before remediation, followed by the Intune implementation, rollback procedure, security implications, and authoritative Microsoft references. This avoids presenting the registry change as a generic fix for every KB5127648 connectivity problem.
